# UI/UX Skill

For any UI or styling work, follow these principles:

- Preserve existing app conventions and approved scope
- Prioritize clear labels, visible feedback, and intuitive navigation
- Ensure semantic and keyboard-accessible UI
- Use visible focus indicators and sufficient contrast
- Support responsive behavior — test at mobile and desktop widths
- Only add the states the feature needs (loading, empty, error, success)
- A simple UI can still be polished and intentional
- Do not add a new design system unless the user asks for one
- Do not add decorative complexity or unnecessary animations
